            "title": "Bridging the Gap, 2022",
            "description": "\"Bridging the Gap\" presents an installation that explores the dichotomy between rational consciousness and embodied experience. The work critiques how human thought—in its tendency to virtualize the world through quantification and measurement—has created a schism between mind and body. Taking inspiration from the mirror test (a scientific method for detecting self-recognition in animals), this installation draws a provocative parallel between humans and dolphins, species that evolved self-awareness through entirely different evolutionary paths. The three-dimensional prints featured in the installation reinterpret the stereotypical evolutionary progression chart, creating a non-linear, directionless flow between these disparate beings. By reconstructing movement as form, the work investigates relationships between part and whole, challenging conventional notions of evolutionary hierarchy and consciousness.",
